fferences between NHANES 1999&#x02013;2000 (<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b6-ehp0115-001596">Calafat et al. 2007</xref>) and NHANES 2003&#x02013;2004 geometric mean concentrations are statistically significant (<italic>p</italic> &#x0003c; 0.001). For PFHxS, except for Mexican Americans (<italic>p</italic> = 0.209), all other differences are also statistically significant with <italic>p</italic> &#x0003c; 0.001, except for females (<italic>p</italic> = 0.037), persons &#x02265; 60 years of age (<italic>p</italic> = 0.016), persons 12&#x02013;19 years of age (<italic>p</italic> = 0.004), and non-Hispanic blacks (<italic>p</italic> = 0.004).</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-wrap></article>